      "name": null,
      "created_at": "2025-08-19T05:49:38.938Z",
      "cooked": "<p>How can I handle a <strong>Purchase Rate Adjustment</strong> ?</p>\n<p>For example, I booked a Purchase Invoice at a certain rate, but later the supplier sent a revised invoice with a lower/higher item rate. Should I use a Debit Note, Landed Cost Voucher, or a Journal Entry for this kind of adjustment?</p>\n<p>I want to make sure both the <strong>supplier ledger</strong> and the <strong>stock valuation</strong> remain correct. What’s the best practice in this case?</p>",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/a/6bbea6/{size}.png",
      "trust_level": 1,
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "like_count": null,
      "like_action": null,
      "Reads": 49,
      "wikis": null,
